@*
    Index.cshtml — the M31 /admin/error-reports GlobalAdmin triage surface
    (ADR 0154, M31·4 / M31·6 / M31·7).

    The GlobalAdmin's read-only listing of the platform-error reports
    (newest first, the IErrorReportService.ListAsync read, M31·4 — no
    per-row IAuthorizationService call, no AccessAudit row) + the idempotent
    mark-as-triaged action (M31·6 — one AccessAudit row per effective
    triage; a second POST on an already-triaged report is a no-op). The
    [Authorize(Roles = GlobalAdmin)] gate is the standard admin surface (the
    AdminOnboardingController shape, ADR 0001-B thin-token rule); no new
    AccessAction / Decide() branch / IAuthorizationService surface (M31·9).

    The copy is the closed errorreport.list.* kw-l key set (keys 9–20,
    M31·7 — the U05 closed set, parity-pinned in four languages, the
    KwLRegistryConsistencyTests + KnownTranslationKeys_ParityTests
    closure). Every label goes through <kw-l> by key (the kw-l TagHelper
    floor, ADR 0015 D1).

    Razor traps honored (AGENTS.md):
      - No <kw-l> inside a quoted attribute value (the status chip uses a
        conditional @if/@else with two separate <kw-l> elements, each with a
        static key, so the KwLRegistryConsistencyTests static scan finds
        both keys).
      - No un-awaited Task<string> in markup (the flash string is
        server-resolved by the controller's FlashAsync, the
        AdminOnboardingController.FlashAsync idiom — the view only renders
        the resolved string).
      - No style=/data-* attributes built by interpolating quoted strings
        via @(...) (the Bootstrap classes are static strings).
*@
@using Kumunita.Core.ErrorReports
@model Kumunita.Web.Models.AdminErrorReportViewModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Admin — Error reports";
}

@* The /admin section sub-nav (the ADR 0062 nav-tabs idiom): top of the
   page — the strip sits just under the navbar (the kmb-tab-under-navbar
   treatment, site.css). *@
@await Html.PartialAsync("_AdminNav.cshtml")

<h1><kw-l key="errorreport.list.title">Error reports</kw-l></h1>

@* The ESC·8 received-issues filter (ADR 0159) — a GET form over
   /admin/error-reports bound to the ?filter= selector (the
   AdminErrorReportViewModel.Filter value, the controller's Index
   [FromQuery] param). The closed set is {"all","received","local"} (the
   controller normalizes an unknown value to "all", the M31·4 unfiltered
   listing shape, ESC·1). The three options use the U07
   escalation.list.filter.* kw-l keys (ESC·11 — the values are U07's to
   author; the en source text in the <kw-l> is the floor, ADR 0015 D1). The
   Inventory/List.cshtml filter-form idiom (a <form method="get"> + a
   <select name="filter"> with a selected= conditional + a submit button) is
   mirrored here. The existing M31/M32 list shape is **unchanged** (ESC·1 —
   the filter is additive). *@
<form method="get" action="/admin/error-reports" class="mb-4">
    <div class="d-flex gap-2 align-items-end flex-wrap">
        <div>
            <label class="form-label" for="error-report-filter" style="font-weight:600;">
                <kw-l key="escalation.list.filter.all">All</kw-l>
            </label>
            <select class="form-select" id="error-report-filter" name="filter">
                <option value="all" selected="@(Model.Filter == "all" ? "selected" : null)"><kw-l key="escalation.list.filter.all">All</kw-l></option>
                <option value="received" selected="@(Model.Filter == "received" ? "selected" : null)"><kw-l key="escalation.list.filter.received">Received</kw-l></option>
                <option value="local" selected="@(Model.Filter == "local" ? "selected" : null)"><kw-l key="escalation.list.filter.local">Local</kw-l></option>
            </select>
        </div>
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-outline-secondary"><kw-l key="common.filter">Filter</kw-l></button>
    </div>
</form>

@* The flash toast (the errorreport.list.flash_triaged key, the U05 closed
   set, M31·7) — rendered when the just-processed MarkTriaged action was
   effective (a "new" → "triaged" transition). The AdminSite/Index.cshtml
   shape: TempData["info"] is a server-resolved string (the controller's
   FlashAsync, the AdminOnboardingController.FlashAsync idiom). A no-op
   (an already-triaged report, M31·6) sets no flash → no alert. *@
@if (TempData["info"] is string info)
{
    <div class="alert alert-success">@info</div>
}

@if (Model.Reports.Count == 0)
{
    <p class="text-muted">
        <kw-l key="errorreport.list.empty">No error reports yet.</kw-l>
    </p>
}
else
{
    <div class="list-group kmb-error-reports-list">
        @foreach (var r in Model.Reports)
        {
            @* The description truncated to 80 chars (the register's U05 pin;
               full text in the title= attribute for hover). The exception
               type truncated to 60 chars (monospace, full text in title=). *@
            var desc      = r.Description ?? "";
            var descShort = desc.Length > 80 ? desc[..80] + "…" : desc;
            var exc       = r.ExceptionType ?? "—";
            var excShort  = exc.Length > 60 ? exc[..60] + "…" : exc;
            <div class="list-group-item">
                <div class="d-flex align-items-start gap-3">
                    @* The status chip (new = text-bg-warning, triaged =
                       text-bg-success, resolved = text-bg-primary — the M31
                       new / triaged precedent + the M32 additive resolved
                       chip, the M32·1 pin). A conditional @if/@else/@else
                       with three separate <kw-l> elements (each with a static
                       key) so the KwLRegistryConsistencyTests static scan
                       finds all three keys (errorreport.list.status.new +
                       errorreport.list.status.triaged +
                       errorreport.list.status.resolved). The existing new /
                       triaged chips are **unchanged** (M32·1 — additive-
                       only). *@
                    @if (r.TriageStatus == "new")
                    {
                        <span class="badge text-bg-warning fw-semibold">
                            <kw-l key="errorreport.list.status.new">New</kw-l>
                        </span>
                    }
                    else if (r.TriageStatus == "triaged")
                    {
                        <span class="badge text-bg-success fw-semibold">
                            <kw-l key="errorreport.list.status.triaged">Triaged</kw-l>
                        </span>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        @* The M32 additive resolved chip (the M32·1 pin — the
                           errorreport.list.status.resolved kw-l key, the
                           M32·9 closed set key 10; the text-bg-primary
                           Bootstrap class — the M31 chip precedent). *@
                        <span class="badge text-bg-primary fw-semibold">
                            <kw-l key="errorreport.list.status.resolved">Resolved</kw-l>
                        </span>
                    }
                    @* The ESC·8 additive "escalated" chip (ADR 0159) — rendered
                       only for a received row (Origin == "escalated"), next to
                       the triage status chip (a received row can be any triage
                       state, so the two chips coexist). The
                       escalation.list.status.escalated kw-l key is the U07
                       closed set (ESC·11 — the value is U07's to author; the
                       en source text here is the floor, ADR 0015 D1). The
                       text-bg-info Bootstrap class (the register's U06 pin —
                       the M32 new / triaged / resolved chip precedent). The
                       existing new / triaged / resolved chips are **unchanged**
                       (ESC·1 — additive-only; the KwLRegistryConsistencyTests
                       static scan finds the new key via its static <kw-l>). *@
                    @if (r.Origin == "escalated")
                    {
                        <span class="badge text-bg-info fw-semibold">
                            <kw-l key="escalation.list.status.escalated">Escalated</kw-l>
                        </span>
                    }
                    <div class="flex-grow-1">
                        @* The exception type (monospace, truncated to 60
                           chars; full text in the title= attribute). *@
                        <div class="small">
                            <span class="text-muted">
                                <kw-l key="errorreport.list.exception">Exception</kw-l>
                            </span>
                            <code title="@exc">@excShort</code>
                        </div>
                        @* The description (truncated to 80 chars; full text
                           in the title= attribute for hover). *@
                        <div class="small mt-1">
                            <span class="text-muted">
                                <kw-l key="errorreport.list.description">Description</kw-l>
                            </span>
                            <span title="@desc">@descShort</span>
                        </div>
                        @* The reporter (the SubjectId, or the
                           errorreport.list.anonymous kw-l key for blank —
                           the register's U05 pin, the §2.3 key 19 note:
                           "the errorreport.list.anonymous key (19) is the
                           display value for a blank SubjectId in the admin
                           list's reporter column"). *@
                        <div class="small mt-1">
                            <span class="text-muted">
                                <kw-l key="errorreport.list.reporter">Reporter</kw-l>
                            </span>
                            @if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(r.SubjectId))
                            {
                                <kw-l key="errorreport.list.anonymous">Anonymous</kw-l>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <span>@r.SubjectId</span>
                            }
                        </div>
                        @* The created timestamp (the kw-dt TagHelper — the
                           house date format, the ADR 0019/0020 surface). *@
                        <div class="small mt-1">
                            <span class="text-muted">
                                <kw-l key="errorreport.list.created">Reported</kw-l>
                            </span>
                            <kw-dt dt="@r.Created" format="g"></kw-dt>
                        </div>
                        @* The request ID (monospace, small — the log
                           correlation handle, the resident's correlation
                           handle on the error page). *@
                        <div class="small mt-1">
                            <span class="text-muted">
                                <kw-l key="errorreport.list.request_id">Request ID</kw-l>
                            </span>
                            <code class="small">@r.RequestId</code>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    @* The "View" detail link (the M32·10 pin — links to the
                       /admin/error-reports/{id} detail view). Always visible
                       (the M31 list's mark-as-triaged button is the only
                       conditional affordance; the View link is additive,
                       the M32·1 pin). The errorreport.list.view kw-l key is
                       a plain link label (a value, not a platform-key in the
                       M32·9 closed set — the en source text is the floor,
                       ADR 0015 D1). *@
                    <a href="/admin/error-reports/@r.Id" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary text-nowrap ms-2 me-0">
                        View
                    </a>
                    @* The "Mark as triaged" button (visible only when
                       TriageStatus == "new" — the register's U05 pin,
                       M31·6 idempotency: a second POST on an already-
                       triaged report is a no-op, no second audit row). A
                       [ValidateAntiForgeryToken] POST to
                       /admin/error-reports/{id}/triage (the
                       AdminOnboardingController.Complete shape). *@
                    @if (r.TriageStatus == "new")
                    {
                        <form method="post" action="/admin/error-reports/@r.Id/triage" class="ms-2 me-0">
                            @Html.AntiForgeryToken()
                            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary text-nowrap">
                                <kw-l key="errorreport.list.mark_triaged">Mark as triaged</kw-l>
                            </button>
                        </form>
                    }
                </div>
            </div>
        }
    </div>
}
